---
title: Refrigerator Dill Pickles
description: Garlicky refrigerator dill pickles in a coriander-spiced brine, at their best after a week in the fridge.
tags: [pickles]
course: condiment
icons: [cucumber, garlic, jar]
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Once Upon a Chef
  url: https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/quick-and-easy-dill-pickles.html
adapted: true
yield: [2%jars, 24%spears]
time: 168h20m
---

Combine the @distilled white vinegar{1 1/4%cup}(5% acidity), @kosher salt{3%tbsp}, and @sugar{2%tbsp} in a small non-reactive #saucepan{} (such as stainless steel, glass, ceramic or Teflon) over high heat. Whisk until the salt and sugar are dissolved.

Transfer the liquid into a #bowl{} and whisk in the @cold water{2%cup}. Refrigerate the brine until ready to use.

Stuff the @Kirby cucumbers{1 3/4-2%lb}(about 6, cut into halves or spears) into two clean 1-quart #jars{}.

Add the @coriander seeds{2%tbsp}, @garlic cloves{6}(large, peeled and halved), @mustard seeds{1%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp}, @dill sprigs{16}, @?whole black peppercorns{}, and chilled brine into the jars, dividing evenly.

If necessary, add a bit of cold water to the jars until the brine covers the cucumbers. Top up each jar with plain tap water, up to a quarter of the jar, to make the brine less acidic and pungent.

Cover and refrigerate about ~chill{7%days}, then serve.

> **Storing** — The pickles will keep in the refrigerator for up to one month.
